# wfg-log 1
# fixture take - a take on a sampling channel: recorded and looped by transport cues,
# its points ridden, a layer laid and undone, kept as a file and kept as a cue, held by
# Esc, looped again by a later mic cue, cleared, and a double Esc (namespace draft 19.3,
# 19.6 and 19.8, 2026-09-27).
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR: that a take's life replays from the document and the log alone, with
# no interface, no recorder and no disk. The standby arm claims Looper for the mic cue
# "Loop voice", whose GO leaves the take waiting (onGo wait). The transport cues Rec and
# Loop it press the take through their GOs - no record of their own - and the recorder's
# close comes back three ticks later as take.closed, in seconds, which is the audio
# side's word, re-injected. The loop points are the channel's session rows, set through
# the tree's door; the layer and its undo are take.overdub, take.loop and take.undo.
# take.keep hands the take to the writer, whose take.kept names the file it found free -
# and for Keep as cue carries the cue, range and route it made, so the replay makes the
# same ones; that edit autosaves, so the replay is given somewhere to save to. Esc lets
# go of the channel and the take is held; GO on "Scene 5 loop" (onGo loop) takes the
# channel and loops the take it found; take.clear empties it and a double Esc ends the
# run. (2026-09-30, namespace draft 23.3: Esc now leaves the standby's arm of "Scene 5
# loop" ready, so a session recorded today would not end it at 515 - the channel would
# pass to it, and GO would launch it; replayed, that logged record still ends it on the
# same tick.) Recorded from a real `wfg serve --hosted --input-wav` of a copy of
# tests/fixtures/bundles/take fed a steady level at its first input, driven over OSC by
# tests/blackbox/phase9c_take.py --keep-log.
# bundle take sha256:4804455ab4d41acd12321e31733699ce7f89eb5c2269225807171501b172af4e
# clock sampleRate=48000 blockSize=128 samplesPerTick=960
